3→                The path may contain a query string. However, neither\n  1214→                `query_string` nor `params` may be specified in this case.\n  1215→\n  1216→    Keyword Args:\n  1217→        root_path (str): The initial portion of the request URL's \"path\" that\n  1218→            corresponds to the application object, so that the application\n  1219→            knows its virtual \"location\". This defaults to the empty string,\n  1220→            indicating that the application corresponds to the \"root\" of the\n  1221→            server.\n  1222→        protocol: The protocol to use for the URL scheme\n  1223→            (default: 'http')\n  1224→        port (int): The TCP port to simulate. Defaults to\n  1225→            the standard port used by the given scheme (i.e., 80 for 'http'\n  1226→            and 443 for 'https'). A string may also be passed, as long as\n  1227→            it can be parsed as an int.\n  1228→        params (dict): A dictionary of query string parameters,\n  1229→            where each key is a parameter name, and each value is\n  1230→            either a ``str`` or something that can be converted\n  1231→            into a ``str``, or a list of such values. If a ``list``,\n  1232→            the value will be converted to a comma-delimited string\n  1233→            of values (e.g., 'thing=1,2,3').\n  1234→        params_csv (bool): Set to ``True`` to encode list values\n  1235→            in query string params as comma-separated values\n  1236→            (e.g., 'thing=1,2,3'). Otherwise, parameters will be encoded by\n  1237→            specifying multiple instances of the parameter\n  1238→            (e.g., 'thing=1&thing=2&thing=3'). Defaults to ``False``.\n  1239→        query_string (str): A raw query string to include in the\n  1240→            request (default: ``None``). If specified, overrides\n  1241→            `params`.\n  1242→        headers (dict): Extra headers as a dict-like (Mapping) object, or a