the values\n  1665→            with a comma when the header in question supports the list\n  1666→            format (see also RFC 7230 and RFC 7231). Header names are not\n  1667→            case-sensitive.\n  1668→\n  1669→            Note:\n  1670→                If a User-Agent header is not provided, it will default to::\n  1671→\n  1672→                    f'falcon-client/{falcon.__version__}'\n  1673→\n  1674→        host(str): A string to use for the hostname part of the fully\n  1675→            qualified request URL (default: 'falconframework.org')\n  1676→        remote_addr (str): A string to use as the remote IP address for the\n  1677→            request (default: '127.0.0.1'). For WSGI, this corresponds to\n  1678→            the 'REMOTE_ADDR' environ variable. For ASGI, this corresponds\n  1679→            to the IP address used for the 'client' field in the connection\n  1680→            scope.\n  1681→        http_version (str): The HTTP version to simulate. Must be either\n  1682→            '2', '2.0', 1.1', '1.0', or '1' (default '1.1'). If set to '1.0',\n  1683→            the Host header will not be added to the scope.\n  1684→        wsgierrors (io): The stream to use as *wsgierrors* in the WSGI\n  1685→            environ (default ``sys.stderr``)\n  1686→        asgi_chunk_size (int): The maximum number of bytes that will be\n  1687→            sent to the ASGI app in a single ``'http.request'`` event (default\n  1688→            4096).\n  1689→        asgi_disconnect_ttl (int): The maximum number of seconds to wait\n  1690→            since the request was initiated, before emitting an\n  1691→            ``'http.disconnect'`` event when the app calls the\n  1692→            receive() function (default 300). Set to ``0`` to simulate an\n  1693→            immediate disconnection without first emitting ``'http.request'``.\n  1694→        extras (dict): Additional values to add to the WSGI\n  1695→            ``environ`` dictionary or the ASG